  "Painted design, BodyA (head, neck, legs, tail, underside): smooth dark-green and brown skin with a fine soft grain and thin dark seam lines; grey-white claws and jaw spikes painted with long streaks; a black beak. BodyB (shared by materials BodyB and BodyC): the shell top (island 1) is green turf with a brown dirt patch, framed by a light grey stone rim and grey stone plates and spikes; the shell underside (island 6) grey stone; the tree canopy is many green clumps painted as soft mottled blobs; the trunk and roots brown with faint long streaks.",
  "So: skin = painted grain only plus soft grooves on the painted seam lines (reptile skin, no scales or pebbles the artist did not paint); claws and spikes = keratin striations along their painted streaks; beak glossy, untouched. Stone = the painted mottling as low relief plus a very soft large undulation, rougher; turf = very short random blades refined from the painted grass speckle; dirt = painted grain, rough; bark = long ridges along the trunk; canopy = crinkled foliage that wraps the painted leaf clumps (curls treatment, species_ext_curls.py), low amplitude.",
  "Neither material binds a normal (manifest normal null): in game only _dif and _par load; the relief is cache-only in BodyA_nor / BodyB_nor and faint as baked cavity in _dif / AO in _par G."
